Some autocallable structures are characterized by a coupon trigger equal to the autocall trigger. In this case, we talk about autocallables with knock-out coupons. Indeed, when a coupon is paid, the product autocalls at the same time since the autocall trigger is breached. Therefore, this structure pays a unique coupon at one of the observation dates during the lifetime of the option. In the case of a coupon level different from the autocall trigger, one talks about autocallables with knock-in coupons, as is the case in the payoff described above. Also note that the coupon level is always lower or equal to the autocall level; otherwise the product doesn't make sense.

