#### Variations

With this basic idea laid out one can think of a whole bunch of variations. We can take other touch options instead of a double-no-touch. We can apply the idea to swaps with a floating leg, to cross currency swaps, swaps with amortization. The only constraint is that the first interest rate payment must be after the expiration of the double-no-touch. Using a deferred delivery allows a combination of rather long term products such as swaps with rather short term products such as double-no-touch options. One can also think of nested ranges with corresponding coupons just like the tower deposits in Section 2.3.6.

